{"name":"Red Herring","hex":"#dd1144","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red herring","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A herring that is cured in smoke and brine strong enough to turn the flesh red; a type of kipper.","A clue, information, argument, etc. that is or is intended to be misleading, diverting attention from the real answer or issue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_herring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kipper","blocks":[{"text":"A kipper is a whole herring that has been split in a butterfly fashion from tail to head along the dorsal ridge, gutted, salted or pickled, and cold-smoked over smouldering wood chips."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Kipper.JPG/330px-Kipper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kipper"},{"title":"Red Herring (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Herring is a media company that at different times has published a magazine about tech innovation, an online daily technology news service, and technology newsletters, and has hosted events for technology leaders."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/25/Red_Herring_2005_08_29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Herring_(magazine)"},{"title":"Red herring","blocks":[{"text":"A red herring is something that misleads or distracts from an important question, a relevant argument, or the solving of a mystery or crime. It may be a deliberate literary device that leads readers or audiences toward a false conclusion, typically in order to heighten suspense or to make a plot twist more shocking, as is common in mystery fiction. It may also be a logical fallacy or a rhetorical strategy used in argumentation, either intentionally or unintentionally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/A_Study_in_Scarlet_Friston_01.jpg/330px-A_Study_in_Scarlet_Friston_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_herring"},{"title":"Herring","blocks":[{"text":"Herring are various species of forage fish, belonging to the order Clupeiformes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Clupea_harengus_Gervais.flipped.jpg/330px-Clupea_harengus_Gervais.flipped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herring"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kipperfactoryseahouses.jpg/330px-Kipperfactoryseahouses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Kipperfactoryseahouses.jpg/330px-Kipperfactoryseahouses.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The fish processing factory in the village of Seahouses, Northumberland, is one of the places where the practice of kippering herrings is said to have originated.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKipperfactoryseahouses.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Red_herring.jpg/500px-Red_herring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Red_herring.jpg/500px-Red_herring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Red herring\": Cold-smoked herring (Scottish kippers), brined and dyed so that their flesh achieves a reddish colour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_herring.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Kippers_at_Burton_Bradstock.jpg/330px-Kippers_at_Burton_Bradstock.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi